# Zig source must have LF line endings: the compiler rejects a carriage
# return outside a string literal, and `zig fmt` reports every CRLF file as
# needing reformatting. Windows checkouts get CRLF by default -- GitHub's
# windows runners ship git with `core.autocrlf = true` -- which turned the
# first CI run's formatting check into a list of every file in the tree.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores text normalised and checks it out that way on
# every platform. Nothing in this repository is meant to hold a CR: the
# parser's tests build their CRLF input from escapes in the Zig source
# rather than from a file, precisely so that no checkout can alter it.
* text=auto eol=lf
